<x-legal-layout :title="'Privacy Policy | InSyte'" :heading="'Privacy Policy'">
    <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> September 8, 2026<br><strong>Last Updated:</strong> September 8, 2026</p>

    <p>This Privacy Policy explains how InSyte CRM ("InSyte", "we", "us", or "our") collects, uses, stores and otherwise processes information when you visit our website, use our software, contact us, request a demonstration, create an account, or use any other services we provide.</p>

    <p>InSyte is a business software platform designed primarily for real-estate channel partners and sales teams. By using our website or Services, you acknowledge that you have read this Privacy Policy.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-black">1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>Depending on how you interact with InSyte, we may collect information you provide directly (such as name, company, email, phone, account and billing details, demo or contact form submissions, and support communications), CRM information entered by customer users (leads, activities, notes, documents, bookings, invoices and related sales data), and technical usage information (such as IP address, browser, device, login activity, pages visited, diagnostics and security-related logs).</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-black">2. Information Received Through Integrations</h2>
    <p>Customers may connect third-party services. Depending on configuration, InSyte may receive information through Facebook Lead Ads, Google Sheets, real-estate portal webhooks, website forms, property microsites, API submissions and other integrations made available through the Services. When a customer connects a third-party service, the customer is responsible for ensuring it has the necessary rights and permissions to transfer that information to InSyte.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-black">3. How We Use Information</h2>
    <p>We may use information to provide and improve the Services, manage accounts and subscriptions, provide support, operate CRM, automation, integration and AI functionality, maintain security, detect misuse, troubleshoot issues, communicate about the Services, and meet legal obligations. We may use aggregated or de-identified information for legitimate business purposes where it does not identify an individual.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-black">4. Customer Data</h2>
    <p>When a company uses InSyte to store information relating to its customers, prospects or other individuals, that company is generally responsible for determining what it collects, why, whether it has the required permissions or legal basis, how it uses the information and how long it retains it. The customer is responsible for ensuring that its use of InSyte complies with applicable law. InSyte processes such information as necessary to provide the Services.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-black">5. AI Services</h2>
    <p>Certain plans may include InSyte AI OS. Available AI functionality may interact with permitted CRM information and perform supported actions such as searching leads, checking the user’s agenda, scheduling or completing follow-ups and site visits, creating or completing tasks and adding notes. AI-generated results may not always be accurate or complete. Users are responsible for reviewing AI-generated information and actions before relying on them where appropriate. Customers should not provide unnecessary sensitive information to AI features.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-black">6. Sharing Information</h2>
    <p>We may disclose information to technology and infrastructure providers, business service providers, payment providers, integration providers when a customer enables an integration, professional advisers, authorities where required by law, and parties involved in a corporate transaction. We do not sell customer CRM data as a standalone product.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-black">7. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>Third-party services operate under their own terms and privacy policies. We do not control their privacy or security practices. Customers are responsible for reviewing relevant third-party terms before enabling an integration.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-black">8. Data Retention &amp; Security</h2>
    <p>We retain information as reasonably necessary to provide the Services, maintain accounts, meet contractual and legal obligations, resolve disputes and protect the Services. We use technical and organizational measures intended to protect information, including tenant isolation and authentication and access controls. No online service can guarantee absolute security. See also our <a href="/security" class="text-brand-accent hover:underline">Security</a> page.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-black">9. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on applicable law, individuals may have rights relating to access, correction, deletion, withdrawal of consent where applicable, grievances and other rights. Requests may be sent to <a href="mailto:legal@insytecrm.com" class="text-brand-accent hover:underline">legal@insytecrm.com</a>. Where information is controlled by an InSyte customer, we may direct the request to that customer.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-black">10. International Processing &amp; Changes</h2>
    <p>Information may be processed in locations outside the country in which you are located, using appropriate safeguards where required. We may update this Policy periodically; the updated version will be posted on this page with a revised effective date.</p>

